# Rank 1026 / CVE-2017-14639: Bento4's visual sample entry parser read the
# compressor name length out of an MP4 file into a signed type:
#
#   char compressor_name[33];
#   stream.Read(compressor_name, 32);
#   int name_length = compressor_name[0];
#   if (name_length < 32) {
#       compressor_name[name_length+1] = 0;
#
# char is signed on the usual platforms, so a length byte of 0x80 or above
# arrives as a negative number, sails through the "< 32" check, and the write
# lands before the start of the buffer (CWE-843 as assigned; the mechanism is a
# signed conversion producing a negative index). The fix 03d1222ab9 declares the
# buffer and the length as AP4_UI08, so the value is 0 to 255 and the existing
# comparison finally means something.
#
# ATTENTION, engine gaps, three of them, and the class is worth the work: this
# is CERT STR34-C, cast characters to unsigned char before converting to a
# larger integer type, not a quirk of this parser.
#
#  - No feature exposes a local's declared type. The whole difference between
#    these two revisions is char versus AP4_UI08 on a local array, and C and C++
#    presence nodes carry only paramType, for parameters, alongside
#    assignOpShape and callArgShape. A binding cannot see the signedness that
#    decides the outcome.
#  - The index guard analysis knows only upper bounds.
#    ccIndexAccessObservations marks guard=upper_bound as soon as an upper-bound
#    comparison exists, and this code has one, so a negative index reads as
#    guarded. There is no lower-bound or signedness notion to fail on.
#  - It observes only structured, field-derived indices. ccStructuredIndex
#    filters to shapes like hdr->len, so a plain local such as name_length+1 is
#    never observed. Both revisions below report nothing at all, which confirms
#    the access is invisible rather than merely judged safe.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-engine-gap

test "rank1026: signed length byte from the file indexes the buffer after only an upper-bound check"
  lang cpp
  file Source/C++/Core/Ap4SampleEntry.cpp
  reject VYQL-MEM-010
  code
  ```
  #include <stdio.h>

  void ReadFields(Stream& stream, const char*& m_CompressorName)
  {
      char compressor_name[33];
      compressor_name[32] = 0;
      stream.Read(compressor_name, 32);
      int name_length = compressor_name[0];
      if (name_length < 32) {
          compressor_name[name_length+1] = 0;
          m_CompressorName = &compressor_name[1];
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1026: fix reads the length as unsigned so the bound check holds"
  lang cpp
  file Source/C++/Core/Ap4SampleEntry.cpp
  reject VYQL-MEM-010
  code
  ```
  #include <stdio.h>

  void ReadFields(Stream& stream, const char*& m_CompressorName)
  {
      unsigned char compressor_name[33];
      compressor_name[32] = 0;
      stream.Read(compressor_name, 32);
      unsigned char name_length = compressor_name[0];
      if (name_length < 32) {
          compressor_name[name_length+1] = 0;
          m_CompressorName = (const char*)(&compressor_name[1]);
      }
  }
  ```
